_model: definition
---
title: Definition 18
---
order: 18
---
short_label: XI.Def.18
---
statement: When a right triangle with one side of those about the right angle remains fixed is carried round and restored again to the same position from which it began to be moved, the figure so comprehended is a <i>cone</i>. And, if the straight line which remains fixed equals the remaining side about the right angle which is carried round, the cone will be <i>right-angled</i>; if less, <i>obtuse-angled</i>; and if greater, <i>acute-angled</i>.
---
group: defXI18_20
